120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (In beginner-level GUI assignments, developers often make the mistake of dumping interface buttons, account balances, and banking rules into one single file. This creates messy, brittle code where fixing a button can accidentally break how money is calculated. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (ApexATM solves this by separating the business logic \(services\) from what the user sees \(UI panels\), ensuring all numbers are checked and validated before balances change. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
